### Editorial decisions that affect interpretation

| Issue in the source or adaptation                                                   | Explicit decision                                                                                               |
| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Printed XOR coefficients and Fig. 2.7 do not consistently reproduce the truth table | Evaluate the printed coefficients without alteration; supply a separately labeled, constructed circuit          |
| Broad claims about what neural networks can compute                                 | Do not turn approximation or computability claims into a guarantee for a specific finite circuit                |
| Training versus learning                                                            | Preserve Sher's usage, while separating update timing from the information used to guide an update              |
| Basic Hebbian weights described as unable to weaken                                 | Explain signed increments and distinguish them from an automatic stabilizing term                               |
| Oja-style stability                                                                 | Show a concrete tanh example; do not assert unconditional stability or a linear PCA result                      |
| Sparse/dynamic graph implementation versus dense tensors                            | Keep the conceptual graph; use tensors only where the chosen representation makes the numerical operation clear |
| Future heterogeneous cognitive systems                                              | Retain as Sher's research vision, not as a proved outcome                                                       |
| GES and runtime-state distinctions                                                  | Identify these as the organizing framework of this remaster                                                     |

**End of Chapter 2.**
